course: dictionary
lesson: 4328
title: Grudge: anger that stays
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A grudge is a feeling of anger or dislike that you keep for a long time against someone who you think treated you badly. The clues around the word show this. «Leo is still angry three weeks after his friend broke his toy, and every time he sees him he feels hot.» Three weeks and every time tell you the anger has stayed for a long time, so a grudge is anger that does not go away.
explain: To hold a grudge means to keep that feeling and not forgive. «You can forgive and still remember the lesson; that isn't a grudge, it's being wise.» Remembering something is not the same as holding a grudge. The grudge is the anger you keep.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Many people feel lighter after letting go of a grudge.» If you put "anger that stays for a long time" in its place, the sentence still makes sense: letting go of that anger makes you feel lighter, so it must be a heavy feeling that weighs you down.
fact: A grudge is anger or dislike kept for a long time against someone who you think treated you badly.
fact: To hold a grudge is to keep that feeling and not forgive.
fact: «Grudge» can also be a verb: to grudge something is to give it or let someone have it unwillingly.
fact: A «grudge match» is a game between rivals.
fact: Letting go of a grudge is a choice, and it can take practice.
exercise: «Leo is still angry three weeks after his friend broke his toy.» What is a grudge? | A quick laugh after a joke | A kind word for a new friend | A toy that is broken | *Anger you keep for a long time against someone who treated you badly
exercise: «Grown-ups can hold grudges for years, sometimes after forgetting what started them.» What does hold a grudge mean? | To forget something completely | To buy a present for someone | To run very fast | *To keep anger and not forgive
exercise: «Countries quarrel over land, power, money, fear and old grudges.» Which word in this sentence means argue? | land | money | power | *quarrel
test: In the lessons, holding a grudge hurts whom most? | Nobody at all | *The person holding it | The other person only | The teacher
test: «A grudge match» is what kind of event? | A sleepy afternoon in the park | A quiet picnic with friends | A school play about the sea | *A game between rivals
exam: Which word means giving something unwillingly? | To forgive | *To grudge | To cheer | To smile
